From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: USA-RedDragon <USA-RedDragon@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 23:30:39 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] feat(gateway): session.background_tool moves a running
 terminal command to the background

A canonical verb that asks the running turn's tool workers to yield, so a
foreground terminal command hands its live process to the background
registry and the turn goes on. Fenced like session.steer (session:control
and the execution generation). tool_call_id narrows it to the worker that
runs that call: tool workers now record their call id per thread.
Advertised as runtime.describe capability tool-background-v1.
