 Managed-worker corrections currently return `unsupported_control`; normal durable
 queue submission and Stop remain separate controls.
 
+`session.background_tool` takes `session_id`, the current `execution_generation`, and an
+optional `tool_call_id`, with the same rights and generation fence as `session.steer`. It
+asks the running turn's tool workers to yield: a foreground terminal command hands its live
+process to the background process registry (notify on complete) and its tool call returns.
+Other tools ignore the request. With `tool_call_id`, only the worker that runs that call is
+asked. The reply is `{status, count, execution_generation, authority_epoch}`: `requested`
+with the number of workers asked, or `none` when no agent runs tools or no worker runs that
+call. Owners that serve it advertise `tool-background-v1` in `runtime.describe`.
+
